# Netlify fallback rules. Kept for deploy portability; the site's own host is
# Apache/nginx (see .htaccess and deploy/nginx.conf).
#
# There is deliberately NO `/* /index.html 200` catch-all any more. Every route
# is prerendered to its own file at build time (dist/services/index.html and so
# on), so real files already answer every valid URL. A catch-all would serve the
# home page's HTML for every path and throw away all of that.
#
# What is left is the dead-end: anything with no file behind it gets a genuine
# 404, not a soft duplicate of the home page.
/*  /404.html  404
